These capabilities are recorded directly in the current changelog, including the relevant xtmux-j46 and xtmux-3xs work. The V2 monitor, telemetry and audit domains, shadow cutover, retention support and final default-on switch are also complete.

The existing xtmux-gaps.md should therefore become a design-history and acceptance document, with each implemented section marked as landed. It should not continue generating duplicate “missing capability” issues.

The remaining xtmux work should be limited to structured activity spans, any still-incomplete handoff lifecycle edge cases, Console materializer consumption, reconnect testing, and later mutation/control functions only after the read-only viewer is proven.

